  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through Wednesday)\nIssued at 1013 PM CST Wed Nov 11 2026\n\nBottom line up front: the extended forecast will be dry and pretty \ncold. Ensure you take care of the 4 P's: People, Pipes, Plants and \nPets before, and during the cold. \n\nLater this weekend, the longwave trough that encompasses most of the\neastern CONUS will side eastward and a southern stream shortwave \nwill start to undercut it from the Southern Plains. This shortwave\nwill slide eastward and early next week a weak sfc low will develop\nin the northern Gulf with an inverted trough. Right now, models are\nkeeping rain chances pretty far to our south, providing a dry\nforecast through Wednesday. \n\nAs for temps, they will drop into the 20s Saturday night/Sunday\nmorning, providing a widespread freeze. Sunday afternoon most likely\nwill not reach 60 degrees before falling below freezing again Sunday\nnight/Monday morning. From here we will be on a very gradual warming\ntrend into mid week, reaching the 60s Wednesday afternoon and most \nof us above freezing Wed night.",
